# ==============================================================================
# ZoeConnect build-time configuration
# ==============================================================================
# CRITICAL FIX (infra vs. app-change classification audit, 2026-08):
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL used to be a literal hardcoded directly inside
# .gitea/workflows/deploy.yml's "Build and Push Image" step. That file is
# classified as `infra` in ci/dependencies.yml (infra.paths includes
# `.gitea/workflows/**`) -- and an infra-only change never triggers an
# image rebuild (see ci/dependencies.yml's own header comment, and
# detect-changes.sh). But docker/zoeconnect.Dockerfile sets this as a
# build ARG/ENV BEFORE `npm run build` runs -- Next.js inlines every
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* variable into the client-side JS bundle at build time, so
# this value genuinely is part of image content, not just deployment
# config. Editing the old hardcoded literal would silently never take
# effect until some unrelated zoeconnect source change happened to trigger
# a rebuild anyway.
#
# Moving the value here fixes that with zero new rule classes: this file
# lives under zoeconnect/, which ci/dependencies.yml's existing
# `zoeconnect: paths: [zoeconnect/**, ...]` rule already covers -- editing
# this file is correctly detected as a zoeconnect change by
# detect-changes.sh exactly like any other file under zoeconnect/, and
# correctly triggers a real rebuild through the existing, unmodified
# incremental-build mechanism. See deploy.yml's "Build and Push Image"
# step, which now reads this file instead of hardcoding the value.
#
# Plain KEY=VALUE, one per line -- sourced directly by deploy.yml's build
# step (`set -a; source zoeconnect/build-args.env; set +a`), same format
# convention as .env.production elsewhere in this repo.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://app.zoeconnect.in
